# Details
If a malicious `admin`  gets blocked by the `SALE_TOKEN` *(mind you: an `admin` is an **UNTRUSTED** role, i.e. basically the first one to call the `ILOManager:initProject(...)` function)*, transfers some `SALE_TOKEN` funds from a different contract to make sure there're funds leftover to trigger the refund **(actually a refund can be triggered even without sending dust funds, as normally `SALE_TOKEN` funds just accumulate in the `ILOPool` contract by default)** and calls `ILOManager:launch(...)`, he'll be able to permanently DoS launching the `ILOPool`s.

If the refund period is initially set as a very high one, then users' funds will be locked for a very long period of time, until they can claim their refunds.


